    "To compute the score, extract all factual claims from the model’s response.",
    "Each claim is compared to the retrieved context and labeled "yes", "no", or "I don't know".",
    ""yes" means the claim is grounded in the context.",
    ""no" means the claim is hallucinated and not from the context.",
    ""I don't know" means the claim is ambiguous or unverifiable.",
    "A claim is considered truthful if it does not contradict any facts in the retrieval context.",
    "Faithfulness score is calculated as grounded claims divided by total claims.",
    "If there are 10 claims and 8 are grounded, the score is 0.8.",
    "Ambiguous "I don't know" claims can be included or excluded, and excluding them can increase the score.",
    "The truth-extraction limit can be changed, which affects the denominator and the ratio."
] 

